  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Do I Need a Permit to Finish My Garage?",
    "text": "Do I Need a Permit to Finish My Garage?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "You might be wondering if you need a permit to finish your garage, and it's a really good question that depends on what you're planning to do! Generally, simple cosmetic upgrades like painting or adding some basic storage shelves won't require one. However, if your project involves more significant changes, like altering the structure, adding new plumbing or major electrical work, or changing the garage's use (say, turning it into a living space), then you're very likely going to need a permit. This is especially true for things like ensuring proper fire-rated separation walls between an attached garage and your home, which is a common local code requirement for safety. It’s all about making sure the work is safe and up to local standards. Skipping permits when they're required can lead to issues down the line, including problems with resale or insurance. If you're unsure about your specific project in Denver, Centennial, or any of the other areas we serve, it’s always best to check with your local building department or chat with a professional like us. We can help you understand the requirements and navigate the permit process.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
